    - rid: 552786097007231206
      type: {class: StringEntry, ns: Unity.Localization, asm: UnityEngine.LocalizationRuntimeModule}
      data:
        m_KeyId: 2572462735369
        m_Metadata:
          m_Items: []
        m_Value: Mac File
    - rid: 552786097007231207
      type: {class: StringEntry, ns: Unity.Localization, asm: UnityEngine.LocalizationRuntimeModule}
      data:
        m_KeyId: 2572462735370
        m_Metadata:
          m_Items: []
        m_Value: The resource fork holds the map's pictures (such as its terminals'), color tables and level script. Save Merged keeps it (but for chapter screens turned off in Level mode), and the Finder's information, as they are, in the same form (such as MacBinary). Save Level (with resources) keeps only what its level uses (its chapter screen, as level 0's, its terminals' pictures, its part of the level script, and the end screens).
